#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119719 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119971 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91583cc4-29ef-5824-baee-f101cbf49be9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Sphere Given Its Radius or Diameter"}] :question/id #uuid "fba82316-1ea7-5c90-88d7-37b96172a7f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-9004" :question/problem "A sphere has a diameter of $3 \\: \\textrm{in}$. Find the surface area of the sphere." :question/worked-solution "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS = 4 \\pi r^2\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nr=\\dfrac{3}{2} \\: \\textrm{in}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nS = 4 \\pi \\left(\\dfrac {3} {2} \\right)^2 = 9\\pi \\: \\textrm{in}^2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119720 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119972 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21358fb6-456e-5ab7-99f4-fc211310df13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius or Diameter of a Sphere Given Its Surface Area"}] :question/id #uuid "e65da51f-3cfc-511a-948c-ba8a46559bba" :question/math-academy-id "e-9005" :question/problem "Calculate the radius of a sphere given that its surface area is $50\\pi \\: \\textrm{cm}^2$.\n\n![](images/99/99bb0ea67859fbd109442fcf698427ea43452087b4523b7202a760a2a8b27052.png)" :question/worked-solution "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS = 4 \\pi r^2\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nS=50\\pi \\: \\textrm{cm}^2\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS &= 4πr^{2} \\\\\n50π &= 4πr^{2} \\\\\n\\frac{50π}{4π} &= r^{2} \\\\\nr^{2} &= \\frac{25}{2} \\\\\nr &= \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{2}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}cm\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119721 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119973 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5161a164-780d-5876-a8e2-458105dc8cab" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Surface Area and Volume of a Sphere"}] :question/id #uuid "acdb3e99-89dd-5463-871e-e4d5d370c827" :question/math-academy-id "e-9008" :question/problem "The volume of the sphere is $\\dfrac{500}{3}\\pi \\: \\textrm{in}^3$. Calculate the surface area of the sphere." :question/worked-solution "We can find the volume of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nV = \\dfrac 4 3 \\pi r^3\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nV=\\dfrac{500}{3}\\pi \\: \\textrm{in}^3\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= \\frac{4}{3}πr^{3} \\\\\n\\frac{500}{3}π &= \\frac{4}{3}πr^{3} \\\\\n\\frac{500π \\cdot 3}{3 \\cdot 4π} &= r^{3} \\\\\nr^{3} &= 125 \\\\\nr &= 5in\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of ​​the sphere is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS &= 4πr^{2} \\\\\n&= 4π(5)^{2} \\\\\n&= 100πin^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119972 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21358fb6-456e-5ab7-99f4-fc211310df13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius or Diameter of a Sphere Given Its Surface Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ea83a1f-cc3f-53b6-838c-2d30120ca185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573439} {:answer/id #uuid "2cceba81-02fd-5fd6-8131-c688c7329053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573477} {:answer/id #uuid "666b540d-c18b-549b-b745-1c60309c84ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573550} {:answer/id #uuid "c7c296d6-623e-518c-8b25-3b4ff32b144f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573683} {:answer/id #uuid "e54e35ce-5d54-524f-bf80-c5b8073d1f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cceba81-02fd-5fd6-8131-c688c7329053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573477} :answer-field/id #uuid "281e4a45-dd35-57e4-a6d0-b0d413cc5c20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b71e39cd-1ccd-551f-bcc4-e9f7fe121c87" :question/math-academy-id "q-107931" :question/problem "A sphere has a surface area of $48\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.$ Calculate the diameter of the sphere." :question/worked-solution "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $S=48\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}$ into the formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 48\\pi  & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{48\\pi }{4\\pi } & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =12 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{in}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the diameter is\n\n$$\nd=2r=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{in}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119973 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5161a164-780d-5876-a8e2-458105dc8cab" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Surface Area and Volume of a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022011de-7f19-5ce1-916b-c7ebb86d7571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573424} {:answer/id #uuid "881394f8-3bd3-500f-895d-a5578ce3ddf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573599} {:answer/id #uuid "b08c11e4-bbc4-5e1f-8e8f-34083122aa5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573654} {:answer/id #uuid "bac69540-9e9d-5b5b-9b52-1e8c447f2fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573664} {:answer/id #uuid "d46231fb-b6d7-59ad-b1f7-9ebad947a791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "022011de-7f19-5ce1-916b-c7ebb86d7571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573424} :answer-field/id #uuid "97beb415-0421-5ab8-b51b-bc4a99823288" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d4951800-9f16-50a9-8666-315cfa908dd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-108136" :question/problem "![](images/ca/ca021f8684431c29f48876fc2a079f9e23931862f37f8f0dd4b1c2f73a87169d.png)\n\nFind the surface area of the sphere above, given that its volume is $\\frac{9}{2}\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the volume of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $V=\\frac{9}{2}\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}$ into the formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{9}{2}\\pi  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{9\\pi \\cdot 3}{2\\cdot 4\\pi } & ={r}^{3} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{27}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{3}}{{2}^{3}} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{3} \\\\ r & =\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{in}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the surface area of ​​the sphere can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\pi {(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =9\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119973 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5161a164-780d-5876-a8e2-458105dc8cab" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Surface Area and Volume of a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e6137c-08d7-5870-aa71-47fb8078f43e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573426} {:answer/id #uuid "513ecb8a-b5ae-51b7-a50f-9e0a620d1aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,728\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573522} {:answer/id #uuid "cc21a208-2c26-5219-9d07-fc975fae7c3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573692} {:answer/id #uuid "dd89fb85-d2f1-51a1-997b-f1ff3eeb2be7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "288\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573714} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4e121c-2a67-59de-9352-52db746c6242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "864\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd89fb85-d2f1-51a1-997b-f1ff3eeb2be7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "288\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573714} :answer-field/id #uuid "b555dfc2-cd7d-5da1-9394-4924278c9c00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "63831384-20c1-5413-ac5c-3dae6cac797c" :question/math-academy-id "q-108139" :question/problem "The surface area of a sphere is $144\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.$ Find the volume of the sphere." :question/worked-solution "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $S=144\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}$ into the above formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 144\\pi  & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{144\\pi }{4\\pi } & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =36 \\\\ r & =6\\,\\text{in}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we  can find the volume of the sphere as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi (6)^{3} \\\\  & =288\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119972 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21358fb6-456e-5ab7-99f4-fc211310df13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius or Diameter of a Sphere Given Its Surface Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0194f7cf-9f36-52a7-880c-8b91ed7deea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573423} {:answer/id #uuid "1b744b2d-6661-59d5-aff2-0f9cc7f3daf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573452} {:answer/id #uuid "27a3b1f5-4916-5997-a0c6-997ac5dabeac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573472} {:answer/id #uuid "73f66d2e-d5bc-56a0-9115-ddfdcab4aeb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573571} {:answer/id #uuid "7ce3bc2f-3111-5489-8199-5140be817370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27a3b1f5-4916-5997-a0c6-997ac5dabeac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573472} :answer-field/id #uuid "36ccf994-900f-5ed9-9ec1-26d429ff1ce8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c989d950-e23f-561f-b2b4-ddaf69734abf" :question/math-academy-id "q-118434" :question/problem "A sphere has a surface area of $25\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}.$ Calculate the diameter of the sphere." :question/worked-solution "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $S=25\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}$ into the formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 25\\pi  & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{25\\pi }{4\\pi } & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\,\\text{mm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the diameter is\n\n$$\nd=2r=2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}=5\\,\\text{mm}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119971 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91583cc4-29ef-5824-baee-f101cbf49be9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Sphere Given Its Radius or Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "112020b7-c1dc-5924-8da3-4c37054614b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573443} {:answer/id #uuid "5ae00c93-811e-560e-982d-32251eead325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "176\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573541} {:answer/id #uuid "82290d27-80fe-55ac-96be-796ef54210d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "121\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573595} {:answer/id #uuid "e6eca556-36c6-53c2-9048-34279f043b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573729} {:answer/id #uuid "ed9afd95-8543-5258-b9d4-d8e9d27ab3e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "484\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82290d27-80fe-55ac-96be-796ef54210d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "121\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573595} :answer-field/id #uuid "149bb160-f7c7-5ff7-9c45-58f490d1c63e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54bc8ffe-b872-5461-a4c1-81ec168d4213" :question/math-academy-id "q-13267" :question/problem "A sphere has a diameter of $11\\,\\text{cm}.$ Find the surface area of the sphere." :question/worked-solution "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $r=\\frac{11}{2}\\,\\text{cm}$ into the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}=121\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119971 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91583cc4-29ef-5824-baee-f101cbf49be9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Sphere Given Its Radius or Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "193af27f-ef2a-5c49-be6a-bc5174756b80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{219}{\\sqrt{3}}\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573449} {:answer/id #uuid "419a40b7-8303-5c5a-91ac-9fc14abccdb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{129\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573504} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdab8d4-c512-5fa2-9dd8-d028c56e60e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "912\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573591} {:answer/id #uuid "900c35df-503b-51ca-9125-1f91465b5eea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "921\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573609} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0e6698-52db-5e35-b740-3d994ffc9ebf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef0e6698-52db-5e35-b740-3d994ffc9ebf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573740} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0905b70-c1b0-5283-9bb4-270ecae6d97f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b24908b-3e08-5600-a3ab-060f182d551c" :question/math-academy-id "q-32654" :question/problem "A sphere has a diameter of $8\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{mm}.$ Find the surface area of the sphere." :question/worked-solution "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $r=\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{2}=4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{mm}$ into the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {(4\\sqrt{3})}^{2}=192\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}.\n$$"}]}
